  "step_1": "The decision reason can be applied to the decision problem. The maximum magnitude outcome for Lottery A is -3000 Euros (absolute value 3000), which occurs with 0.2% probability. For Lottery B, the maximum magnitude outcome is -6000 Euros (absolute value 6000), occurring with 0.1% probability. The more favorable maximum magnitude outcome is the one with the smaller loss (i.e., less negative), which is -3000 in Lottery A. However, the reason specifies that the maximum magnitude outcome should be weighted by its probability. Comparing the two: for A, the weighted magnitude is |−3000| × 0.002 = 6; for B, it is |−6000| × 0.001 = 6. Thus, both lotteries have the same weighted magnitude of the worst outcome (6), so the reason would be indifferent between them. The decision reason evaluates the worst-case outcome in absolute terms, weighted by probability, and prefers the lottery with the lower (more favorable) value of this product.",
